  "live_records": {
    "q-7360": {
      "dom_id": "step-q7360",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178562/assets/76cd6a4f07d424a3ce8ae6d2f939e52f5aa2fc66331f671c4b926b1ee5fdae8c.png)\n\nWhich of the following best describes the slope of the graph above?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that slope is the amount the line rises vertically per unit that it runs horizontally.\n\nSince the graph decreases ($↘$) as we go from left to right, the line rises by a negative amount.\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is negative.",
