      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178562/assets/d459697b7a62f75b89093ab5d12ec9b2087f4d4854cbb91ad7fffab8d13a02d1.png)\n\nFind the slope of the line shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "The slope of the vertical line is undefined. We can see this by choosing two points on the line, such as $(-1,0)$ and $(-1,1),$ and computing the slope between them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}=\\frac{1-0}{-1-(-1)}=\\frac{1-0}{-1+1}=\\frac{1}{0}=\\text{undefined}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
